{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Cursed be their anger.</b> This is not a curse but a blessing — that is, may it be His will that they not succeed in their anger, so that they not grow accustomed to being hot-tempered. Another interpretation: <b>cursed be their anger</b> — like 'cursed and despised is their anger,' their brazen and harsh wrath.'" "<b>I will divide them in Jacob.</b> For so we find that the inheritance of Simeon fell within the inheritance of the tribe of Judah, as it is written: ״ויצא הגורל לשמעון בתוך נחלת בני יהודה״, and the lot of Levi fell to forty-eight cities for dwelling, and their pasturelands within the inheritance of every tribe."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:09.889241982Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}